INT: But she was a prisoner, this woman?

EL: Yes.

INT: Jewish?

EL: Had to be. But they were-- they built. They were Slovakians. They were taken the first, the Slovakians and the Polish. So she was either Polish or Slovakian. And they were there already, by then, two, three years. So you, you have no feelings left. You have no-- by then, they were--

INT: When you returned to Auschwitz, and--

EL: I--

INT: And your thoughts then?

