INT: And going from Oberschlesien to Georgenthal, you--

EL: Yeah, we walked, all the way, all the way. By 19-- but by then, I turned 19. And I slept. Just stand there one night, when we were put up, let's say, in a school, in a barn, once in a small church, that night we didn't really-- there was nowhere.

INT: And what did you see along the road?

EL: So we just slept in the snow in the-- on the side of the road. That was [INAUDIBLE]. What-- what did we see? People.

In one town-- that must have been already in-- in-- in Sudetenland. This one town, we were, like, in the center of the town. I remember it was a circle there. And we're walking.

And this window opens up. And this woman is-- wants to throw down some-- had to be some food. And the soldier goes-- [PAUSES FOR 3 SECONDS] how did he say that in German? I forgot already.

